First let me say I have nothing but respect for and gratefulness to Robin
and all others running this tournament yearly.  They do it for nothing and
it's WAY cool and fun, fun, fun.

What follows is in no way a criticism of these guys (and gals?).

As I played my latest tournament entry steveyo the rogue (currently high
score, but also dead), I was torn as how to play the character.  Should I
just go for ascension, or the actual rogue high score?  Obviously the point
is now moot, as I had lapsed into apathy due to my quandry and died not
watching dwindling HPs.

Last year, only caveman, rogue and ranger had winning scores under
25,000,000.  That high a score is either quasi-extinctionist (cast CM over
and over), or uses the strategies of repeated killing the toughest monsters.
Both become boring after a while to me.   Though extinctionist can be fun
poly-piling and over-enchanting stuff, I find no enjoyment or challenge in
stoning and stone-to-fleshing Demogorgon 100(000) times in a row.

